# Sensitive data - NEVER commit these!
*.key
*.pem
# Keeps peer configs (which carry private keys) out of the repo. Note this is
# broad: it silently swallowed a shipped rsyslog rule once, which committed and
# pushed cleanly while being absent from every fresh clone. Nothing the repo
# ships is a .conf any more -- the rsyslog rule and logrotate policy are written
# by install-logging.sh rather than shipped -- so if you ever add one, check
# `git check-ignore -v <file>` before assuming it is tracked.
*.conf
privatekey*
publickey*
*.qr
*.png

# Exception: Keep example configs
!example.conf
!*.example.conf
